WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.029
This is the height of idiocy, but it appears
that Republicans are using former NFL

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:10.100
quarterback Colin Kaepernick's image for a
fundraising email and that they've digitally

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.330
darkened his skin to make him look a blacker
in the ad.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.480
This is the NRCC, which is the National Republican
congressional committee.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.920
They sent out an email on Wednesday and it
was all about the American flag.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.340
Who Do you stand with?

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:33.039
The Ad Asks Donald Trump and the Betsy Ross
flag or anti American flag Colin Kaepernick.

00:00:33.039 --> 00:00:35.780
Before we even look at what they did to Kaepernick
skin.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.289
I just want to remind you that this entire
flag controversy is so stupid.

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:45.300
I mean, it's really depressing that this flag
issue would even be an issue to fundraise

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.010
around and that the right even cares about
this.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.109
That's a really sad commentary on our country.

00:00:51.109 --> 00:00:55.409
Most of you probably already know and understand
that, but then we get to the skin color issue.

00:00:55.409 --> 00:00:59.559
When you look side by side at the original
picture and the version of it that was used

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:05.470
in this Republican ad, you can see that Colin
Kaepernick skin clearly seems much darker

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:06.470
in the picture.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:07.590
That's included in the ad in particular.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:14.100
When you look at his forearm now, the NRCC
was asked about this, they are claiming it

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.670
was not darkened.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:22.079
What I hate about this is that this is actually
not a new tactic, but that it appears to actually

00:01:22.079 --> 00:01:23.079
work.

00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:24.079
Okay.

00:01:24.079 --> 00:01:26.359
This has been studied in the 2008 campaign.

00:01:26.359 --> 00:01:31.940
The McCain campaign was also caught darkening
Barack Obama skin when they published attack

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:32.940
ads.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:38.289
And there was a study done in 2015 which found
that darkening the skin of political opponents,

00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:44.039
as stupid as it sounds to many of us actually
impacts the impressions of voters about the

00:01:44.039 --> 00:01:45.039
candidates.

00:01:45.039 --> 00:01:46.390
And this isn't just republicans who do it.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:51.601
The Hillary Clinton campaign in 2008 was also
accused of darker darkening Barack Obama's

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:52.909
skin in ads.

00:01:52.909 --> 00:01:58.470
So the underlying idea is that no matter who
you are, that's running, no matter who you're

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:03.631
running against, whether it's a democratic
woman, a Republican man, the idea is there.

00:02:03.631 --> 00:02:10.060
There's an unconscious bias that is strongest
against the darkest people, a people with

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.160
the darkest skin tone.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.160
And this is called colorism.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.190
I mean, this is not a new concept.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.650
So it seems that it's an effective thing to
do, shockingly enough.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:22.470
So there's a few different things that should
make us, I guess I would say sad here.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.420
It's sad that political candidates would do
this.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:28.990
They do it and they do it because it's work
because it works.

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:32.120
And that's actually the saddest part for me.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:37.661
And then the absolutely dumbest part of this
goes way beyond darkening Colin Kaepernick

00:02:37.661 --> 00:02:38.780
